# Au Clair de la Lune (repertoire plan: au-clair-de-la-lune). The first verse, in A A B A form.
# The A phrase lives on strings 3 and 2: the open string 3 (G), string 3 fret 2 (A) and the open
# string 2 (B). On day one, play only the first section. The B phrase drops to string 4: the open
# string (D), fret 2 (E) and fret 4 (F#). The hand stays in second position, as in Hot Cross Buns:
# finger 1 on fret 2, finger 3 on fret 4. The teacher strums G and D7 under the A phrases, D and
# A7 under the B phrase.
title: Au Clair de la Lune
id: au-clair-de-la-lune
composer: Traditional French
source: French song of the 18th century, first verse in French; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 1
tags: melody, two strings, lyrics, french, beginner
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: G

